0..71 Comment "//! A map whose loop arm is the named loop, and its action on the loop."
72..75 Comment "//!"
76..152 Comment "//! The action of a map on the loop is the image of the loop under the map\'s"
153..231 Comment "//! loop arm. The kernel must compute that image as the checker does, whatever"
232..308 Comment "//! the form of the arm. Otherwise the kernel refuses a declaration that the"
309..329 Comment "//! checker accepts."
330..333 Comment "//!"
334..412 Comment "//! `keepNamed` sends the loop to the named `loop`, and `keepWord` sends it to"
413..493 Comment "//! the word `loop ∷ Path.here Base`. Each declaration relates an image of the"
494..567 Comment "//! loop to the loop by reflexivity. Some start the transport at the call"
568..621 Comment "//! `keepNamed Base`, and some start it at the point."
622..625 Comment "//!"
626..642 Comment "//! - see: #5489"
643..729 Comment "//! - see: `circle-elim.gandr` — the transports along the loop that both sides admit"
